    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.1038/s41467-018-08240-4",
    "abstract": null,
    "field": "Geocryology",
    "problem": "The absence of a standardized, globally consistent assessment of permafrost temperature change has hindered its adequate representation in climate models and prevented a comprehensive evaluation of its contribution to global warming.",
    "method": "This study evaluates permafrost warming by compiling a global dataset of borehole temperature time series from 2007 to 2016 and calculating area-weighted mean temperature changes near the depth of zero annual amplitude for different permafrost zones.",
    "task": "The task is to use a global data set of permafrost temperature time series from the Global Terrestrial Network for Permafrost to evaluate temperature change across permafrost regions for the reference decade between 2007 and 2016.",
