    "obs_and_metrics": [],
    "innovation": "This paper provides the first globally consistent assessment of recent permafrost warming by analyzing a global dataset of borehole temperatures, quantifying a mean global temperature increase of 0.29 \u00b1 0.12 \u00b0C for the decade 2007\u20132016.",
    "kg_extraction_triplets": [
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "thermistor",
            "source_entity_type": "Instrument",
            "relation": "MEASURES_VARIABLE",
            "target_entity_instance": "Temperature",
            "target_entity_type": "Variable",
            "paragraph": "Field observations of permafrost temperatures. Boreholes were established and temperatures were recorded during annually repeated fieldwork campaigns in polar and high-elevation areas. Temperature was measured either by lowering a calibrated thermistor into a borehole, or recorded using permanently installed multi- sensor cables43. Measurements were recorded either manually with a portable temperature system or by automated continuous data logging.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Permafrost degradation",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Antarctica",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "During the reference decade between 2007 and 2016, ground temperature near the depth of zero annual amplitude in the continuous permafrost zone increased by 0.39 \u00b1 0.15 \u00b0C. Over the same period, discontinuous permafrost warmed by 0.20 \u00b1 0.10 \u00b0C. Permafrost in mountains warmed by 0.19 \u00b1 0.05 \u00b0C and in Antarctica by 0.37 \u00b1 0.10 \u00b0C. Globally, permafrost temperature increased by 0.29 \u00b1 0.12 \u00b0C.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Permafrost degradation",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Arctic",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "The largest increase of T over the observed reference decade between 2007 and 2016 was 0.39 \u00b10.15 \u00b0C_dec_in_the Arctic continuous permafrost zone.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Permafrost degradation",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Northern Hemisphere",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "Globally, permafrost temperature increased by 0.29 \u00b1 0.12 \u00b0C. The observed trend follows the Arctic amplification of air temperature increase in the Northern Hemisphere.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Permafrost degradation",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Siberia",
            "target_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "paragraph": "The greatest permafrost temperature changes observed in individual boreholes (AT) since 2008-2009 were 0.93 and 0.90 \u00b0C in northwestern Siberia (Marre Sale, 10 m) and northeastern Siberia (Samoylov Island, 20.75 m), respectively. The discontinuous permafrost zone experienced warming of 0.20\u00b10.10 \u00b0C decref. The largest AT, since 2008-2009 of 0.95 \u00b0C was observed in southeastern Siberia, Magadan (Olsky pass, 10 m).",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Permafrost degradation",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Asia",
            "target_entity_type": "Continent",
            "paragraph": "On average, permafrost across zones warmed by 0.33 \u00b1 0.16 \u00b0C over the reference decade in northern Asia and by 0.23 \u00b1 0.11 \u00b0C decref in North America.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Permafrost degradation",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "North America",
            "target_entity_type": "Continent",
            "paragraph": "On average, permafrost across zones warmed by 0.33 \u00b1 0.16 \u00b0C over the reference decade in northern Asia and by 0.23 \u00b1 0.11 \u00b0C decref in North America.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": true,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Permafrost degradation",
            "source_entity_type": "Natural_Hazard",
            "relation": "AFFECTED_REGION",
            "target_entity_instance": "Alaska",
            "target_entity_type": "Country_Subdivision",
            "paragraph": "It was shown previously that a difference of only 10 days caused significant warming in Alaska35.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
            "evidence_validated": true,
            "valid": false,
            "eval": true
        },
        {
            "source_entity_instance": "Arctic",
            "source_entity_type": "No_Country_Region",
            "relation": "HAS_CLIMATE_ZONE",
            "target_entity_instance": "Polar",
            "target_entity_type": "ClimateZone",
            "paragraph": "This is important, because over the past few decades, the atmosphere in polar and high elevation regions has warmed faster than elsewhere.",
            "ontology_conformed": true,
